# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sky130-modexp #154: the Curator heartbeat-idempotency fix. Root-caused live
# on this repo's issue #12, which collected 44 `curator:operator-premise-
# recheck` comments in a month (27 of 43 gaps under the 24h window, minimum 23
# minutes). `dep-recheck-fingerprint.sh decide` was NOT wrong -- the prior
# marker handed to it was. 19 of the 22 post-2026-09-11 spam comments name the
# same predecessor, "2026-09-10 12:46 UTC", which is exactly that thread's 30th
# comment: page one of `GET /issues/{n}/comments` at its default per_page=30.
#
# The fix is two things, both of which live in the installed copies because the
# arithmetic they feed is upstream Rust (`loom-daemon/src/dep_recheck/`):
#   1. a pagination-safe, fail-closed prior-marker reader, and
#   2. a confirm-under-claim re-decide in curator.md's two idempotency paths,
#      so two concurrent passes cannot both conclude "reportable".
# #172 audit: upstream curator.md now reads the prior marker with
# `gh api --paginate`, which covers the page-boundary shape, but it has no
# fail-closed reader (dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh has no upstream counterpart)
# and no confirm-under-claim re-decide, so item 2 and the fail-closed read are
# still local. Upstream PR: none yet -- the reader belongs in
# defaults/scripts/ and the prompt change in defaults/commands/loom/curator.md
# (tracked in sky130-modexp#172).

# scripts/dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh: the new reader (no upstream counterpart
#   yet, so an unpinned resync would ORPHAN/remove it, not merely revert it).
scripts/dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh

# scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh: the hermetic regression suite
#   (replays #12's page-boundary shape; wired into this repo's own CI).
# scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-heartbeat-race.sh: the two-concurrent-passes
#   scenario, driving the real `decide` (needs a built loom-daemon).
scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh
scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-heartbeat-race.sh

# scripts/tests/ci-wired.txt / ci-excluded.txt: pinned ONLY because the two
#   suites above must stay listed in exactly one of them
#   (check-ci-suite-manifest.sh enforces that partition). Without the pin a
#   resync reverts the manifests while the pinned suites survive, leaving that
#   checker failing on files it cannot classify. Retire these two pins in the
#   same change that retires the suites' own pins.
scripts/tests/ci-wired.txt
scripts/tests/ci-excluded.txt

# roles/curator.md + commands/loom/curator.md: the same file, installed twice.
#   Both carry the "prior-marker read must be COMPLETE" and "Confirm under the
#   claim" rules; pinning only one would leave the other reverted and the two
#   copies silently disagreeing about the claim protocol.
roles/curator.md
commands/loom/curator.md

# hooks/guard-loom-workflow.sh: installed-file-write target normalization
# honors a single same-command `cd` into a scratch dir, fail-closed: only the
# exact `VAR=$(mktemp -d) && ... && cd $VAR && <writes>` chain, VAR never
# otherwise assigned, no symlink/relocation tools -- so fixtures built in a
# scratch tree's own .loom/ subtree are not falsely denied while real writes
# to the installed tree stay denied. Tracking: 2AMLogic/sky130-modexp#158;
# upstream report rjwalters/loom#9154 (still open, no fix in defaults/ as of
# the #172 audit). No upstream PR yet -- remove this pin once the fix lands.
hooks/guard-loom-workflow.sh
hooks/tests/test-guard-installed-write-cd-tracking.sh
